1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:08,133
Hey, Konta, things are bad.
I might end up unemployed.

2
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:09,342
<i>Then you can go.</i>

3
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:11,094
To Grandma's villa!

4
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:12,595
Shall we go then?

5
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:13,930
On our…

6
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,515
Vacation!

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,144
Konta, look! The ocean!

8
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:21,104
Wow, it's so close!

9
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:23,648
<i>To think we would end up</i>
<i>spending a vacation together</i>

10
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:26,276
<i>at such a wonderful seaside villa.</i>

11
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:27,694
Konta, summer oranges!

12
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:29,946
<i>I wonder if Grandma liked summer oranges.</i>

13
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:30,822
Thank you, Grandma.

14
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:36,036
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>
<i>I'm the caretaker, Nishigami.</i>

15
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,746
S-So handsome.

16
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,040
<i>Those villa grounds</i>
<i>are under your jurisdiction.</i>

17
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,916
<i>You do know that in one month,</i>

18
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,254
<i>a landslide caused by a massive typhoon</i>
<i>will kill all the residents, correct?</i>

19
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,718
Wow!

20
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:53,553
Hey, Konta!

21
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:55,930
The ocean in the morning is so beautiful!

22
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,766
- Morning.
- Morning.

23
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:00,935
This is the best.

24
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:04,731
I might just live here forever.

25
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:08,526
I'll squeeze yesterday's summer oranges
and make you some juice!

26
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:10,153
What? No way, those are sour!

27
00:01:10,236 --> 00:01:12,363
I'll make sure to put honey in it.

28
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:14,407
You'll put honey in it?
You're so kind, Midori!

29
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:16,367
You're so sweet.

30
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:24,751
What?

31
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:27,253
Who could that be?

32
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:29,964
Yes?

33
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,092
- We came.
- We came.

34
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,844
What?!

35
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,848
SIX MONTHS AGO

36
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:42,811
Wow, a villa! That's amazing, you're rich!

37
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,687
Is it near the ocean? Can you go by train?

38
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:46,815
I want to go! When can I come?

39
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:49,776
My dad gave me the key,
so we can use it anytime.

40
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:53,655
But you two can't take
time off work, right?

41
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:55,657
You don't have the same days off either.

42
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:58,368
We've barely seen each other
since starting work.

43
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:01,412
We used to be together
almost every day in college.

44
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:05,500
But once you become an adult,
it's hard to make time for that.

45
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,460
I'll just quit my part-time job.

46
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:08,378
What?

47
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:10,505
I was just thinking about quitting anyway.

48
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:12,757
It just feels uncomfortable there somehow.

49
00:02:12,841 --> 00:02:14,342
No, Tsumugi.

50
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:17,887
You really shouldn't choose jobs
based on comfort.

51
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:20,181
We're 28, you know.

52
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:24,227
My temp contract ends this month too,
so if I want to take a break, I can!

53
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:27,188
Do you guys have any intention
of actually working?

54
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:31,109
In this day and age,
isn't it foolish to work so hard?

55
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:34,028
<i>The pay is low, prices are up…</i>

56
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:36,990
It's fine for us
since we live with our parents,

57
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:39,242
but it must be tough
for people living on their own.

58
00:02:39,325 --> 00:02:41,661
More and more people around me
are saying it's better

59
00:02:41,744 --> 00:02:43,746
to hunt for a husband
and just get married.

60
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:48,751
Oh, I want to get married too.
I want to be a housewife!

61
00:02:49,419 --> 00:02:54,257
Apparently that's increasing in America,
and the "tradwife" phenomenon is popular.

62
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,427
There could be hot guys
if it's a villa near the ocean.

63
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,804
Oh, hot guys! I want to go so bad!

64
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,431
Come on, now.

65
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,516
Calm down, both of you.

66
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:08,771
I quit my part-time job.

67
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:10,815
My temp contract ended.

68
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:18,781
So, all of us are unemployed,

69
00:03:19,449 --> 00:03:22,368
and on a vacation from life, right?

70
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,246
Right?

71
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,333
- Excuse us.
- Excuse us.

72
00:03:28,416 --> 00:03:31,085
Wow! What is this place?
It's absolutely amazing!

73
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:32,170
Wait!

74
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,964
- This is awesome!
- Don't drag your suitcase!

75
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,092
Get us some alcohol.

76
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:40,136
What? It's still morning!

77
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:43,431
Huh? What? Are you Midori's friends?

78
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:45,725
Oh, you haven't met them, right?

79
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:48,645
They're my friends from college,
Tsumugi and Rinrin.

80
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:50,104
Nice to meet you!

81
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:53,191
You're an actor, aren't you?

82
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:55,193
Midori's told us about you.

83
00:03:57,528 --> 00:03:58,988
Hello.

84
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:01,449
I'm the actor and performer, Konta.

85
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:05,411
Konta Hoshino.

86
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:11,042
I heard from Midori
that you're mainly working as an extra.

87
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:15,088
Well, extras live as the character too,
so they are actors. Just so you know.

88
00:04:15,171 --> 00:04:16,005
You're an extra.

89
00:04:16,089 --> 00:04:18,258
I'm an extra, but since I live
as the character, I'm an actor.

90
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:20,510
- He's an extra!
- For me…

91
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,095
- I'm more of a performer.
- Move.

92
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,680
- Move!
- Hey!

93
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:26,391
Here you go! Juice made
from the garden's summer oranges!

94
00:04:26,474 --> 00:04:28,017
- Wow!
- Yes!

95
00:04:28,101 --> 00:04:30,812
Thank you both for coming all this way!

96
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:33,856
- Oh, it's good!
- Delicious!

97
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:34,983
What is this?

98
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:36,901
I'll add alcohol later
and make sours for you too.

99
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:39,779
- Really?
- So! Let's have a barbecue tonight!

100
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:42,573
- Yay!
- Vacations are the best!

101
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,617
The best!

102
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:18,985
Is it here? It's here.

103
00:05:19,777 --> 00:05:20,737
It's here.

104
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:23,865
It's here!

105
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:29,746
Yes, this way, come along.

106
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:30,955
This way.

107
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,957
What? Someone else is here too?

108
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:34,584
This is my friend, Tetsuro.

109
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:37,879
He's the same age as me, 33. We met
way back when working part-time as movers.

110
00:05:37,962 --> 00:05:39,714
He's not an actor.

111
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:41,799
Come on, Tetsuro. Help us out.

112
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,593
A barbecue needs a man's strength!

113
00:05:43,676 --> 00:05:47,346
Wow, nice to meet you! I'm Rinrin.

114
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,515
Stop flirting with everyone.

115
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:52,685
Tetsuro, for now,
could you help over here?

116
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:53,853
We need to start the fire--

117
00:05:53,936 --> 00:05:54,771
Oh, right!

118
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:56,981
Could you pick up some branches
around here to burn?

119
00:05:57,065 --> 00:05:58,566
We have charcoal, but not firewood.

120
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:00,443
All right, put your bag down.

121
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:01,569
- Branches.
- Branches?

122
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:02,987
- Yes, go on.
- Branches?

123
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,322
Branches?

124
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:05,990
Branches.

125
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,911
He seems weird.

126
00:06:09,994 --> 00:06:10,953
He's an introvert.

127
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:13,456
Is he staying here too?
He's kind of scary.

128
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,168
Huh?

129
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:18,086
What?

130
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:20,338
Why won't it burn?

131
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:22,465
It's impossible without something
like a fire starter.

132
00:06:22,548 --> 00:06:26,385
We bought charcoal at the store,
but you didn't buy a fire starter! Idiot!

133
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,013
Don't call me an idiot!

134
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:32,809
I haven't done many barbecues.
This is my first time starting a fire.

135
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:35,061
Because for me, my acting work…

136
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:36,562
I was busy with my acting

137
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:39,148
so I didn't have time for this thing!
I was too busy acting.

138
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,650
Liar!

139
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:43,319
You were just lazing around
at our parents' house.

140
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:46,656
Wait, you still live
with your parents at that age?

141
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:48,533
What's wrong with that?
Their house is in Tokyo.

142
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:49,826
It's convenient.

143
00:06:52,161 --> 00:06:53,871
I got the branches.

144
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:56,582
Oh, nice. If we burn these
and get some momentum,

145
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:57,500
it might work.

146
00:06:57,583 --> 00:06:58,459
These branches…

147
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:01,796
He kind of seems like a good person.

148
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,840
Maybe he's just shy.

149
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:06,467
Let's make that guy
pick up branches forever from now on.

150
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:17,311
Damn it!

151
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:20,606
It won't catch fire!

152
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:24,485
The meat and vegetables are all ready.
All we have to do is grill them!

153
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:27,530
Konta, can't you even
get a fire going quickly?

154
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:28,489
Midori, I'm sorry.

155
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:31,617
Oh!

156
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:34,203
Huh?

157
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:40,376
More people are here.

158
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,712
Oh, Mr. Nishigami! Perfect timing!

159
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:45,256
Help us start the fire!
We've been trying for a while,

160
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,049
but it's impossible
without a fire starter.

161
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:49,093
Midori, who is this handsome guy?

162
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:51,220
Is he going to join our barbecue too?

163
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:54,724
Oh, no, this is Mr. Nishigami,
who takes care of the villas around here.

164
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:56,225
Mr. Nishigami!

165
00:07:58,561 --> 00:08:00,062
Nice to meet you, Mr. Nishigami.

166
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:02,607
I'm Midori's best friend, Rinrin.

167
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,484
I'm also her best friend, Tsumugi.

168
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,819
Wait, you two are swooning too much!

169
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:08,571
What will you have to drink?

170
00:08:08,654 --> 00:08:11,699
There's summer orange juice,
and we made a sour cocktail too.

171
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:14,660
Wow, you're so tall. How tall are you?

172
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,996
Come on, you two,
you're making him uncomfortable!

173
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,956
- I'm going to go touch up my makeup.
- What?

174
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,917
- Me too!
- Well, in that case…

175
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,587
I'll get a summer orange sour for you.

176
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,507
What the hell? In the end,
you're those types of women!

177
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:30,092
Those types who judge a person
by their looks!

178
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:32,178
Even though we're working so hard.

179
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:36,224
Mr. Nishigami, do you have
a fire starter? I forgot to buy one!

180
00:08:36,307 --> 00:08:37,725
We must not have enough branches.

181
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:39,435
Let's go pick some up! Let's go!

182
00:08:40,061 --> 00:08:43,189
Branches? More branches?

183
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:10,383
Mr. Nishigami!

184
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:13,010
Please have some summer orange sour.

185
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:14,178
Here we go.

186
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:19,183
Whoa! The fire is lit already.

187
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,810
You're good.

188
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:22,478
Thank you very much.

189
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:23,479
Here.

190
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:26,607
No thank you, I'm…

191
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:31,654
It has a bit of alcohol in it,
but your work is done for today, right?

192
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,431
Hey, no fair!

193
00:09:58,514 --> 00:10:02,101
I want to toast with him too.

194
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:03,644
Let's drink!

195
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:05,771
We're going to drink a ton tonight!

196
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:10,651
Wow, fire! Yes!

197
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,486
We don't need branches anymore.

198
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:16,115
Mr. Nishigami! Thank you! Good job!

199
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,992
Well then, everyone…

200
00:10:27,835 --> 00:10:30,671
Cheers!

201
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:36,302
- It's great!
- Let's eat.

202
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:38,721
- Is the meat done?
- It's cooking.

203
00:10:38,804 --> 00:10:40,306
Here you go.

204
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:41,891
Mr. Nishigami, have some.

205
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:43,684
It's only cheap meat, though.

206
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,936
- That's true.
- Wait a minute, everyone.

207
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,438
Let's take a photo before we eat.

208
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:50,149
- Yes, let's take a photo.
- Oh, nice!

209
00:10:50,232 --> 00:10:52,318
Mr. Nishigami, over here.

210
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:55,988
- All right, let's go.
- Over here, like this.

211
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,531
Everyone, line up.

212
00:10:57,615 --> 00:10:59,200
- All right!
- Nice.

213
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:01,619
- Wait, will we all fit?
- Is everyone in frame?

214
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:03,579
- Front or back camera?
- Front.

215
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:04,705
Front camera.

216
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:05,790
Ten seconds.

217
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:07,083
- Okay.
- Okay.

218
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:09,460
- Ten seconds.
- Ten seconds, okay.

219
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:13,631
Ten, nine, eight, seven,

220
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:17,385
six, five, four, three,

221
00:11:17,468 --> 00:11:19,178
two, one…

222
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,690
Watch out!

223
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:34,068
Villas are so fun.

224
00:11:36,278 --> 00:11:38,656
Tetsuro, what kind of work
are you doing now?

225
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:42,201
When I have acting work,
I'm thinking of commuting from here,

226
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:44,078
so you should come anytime too!

227
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:47,456
You can't run a villa
without a man's strength.

228
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,333
Pick up some firewood for me!

229
00:11:50,042 --> 00:11:53,379
I think I might stay
at this villa all summer too.

230
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:56,257
A vacation from life, as they call it?

231
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,926
Yes, we've been working hard
for a long time.

232
00:11:59,009 --> 00:12:00,302
We should rest once in a while.

233
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:02,680
- Did you ever work hard?
- What?

234
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:05,015
Maybe I should pick up firewood too.

235
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:06,892
Exactly!

236
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:09,395
Let's all spend this summer here together!

237
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:13,190
It's fine to have that kind of summer
at least once in your life!

238
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:17,194
I just happen to not have
any acting work right now.

239
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:18,988
You're off all year round, more like it.

240
00:12:19,071 --> 00:12:21,115
I know you get an allowance from Dad.

241
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:23,367
An actor has to keep their schedule open

242
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:25,327
so they can take a big role
whenever it comes!

243
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:27,163
Anyway! Here.

244
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:31,417
To everyone's vacation from life,

245
00:12:32,126 --> 00:12:33,544
cheers!

246
00:12:33,627 --> 00:12:36,297
Cheers!

247
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:42,219
Wait.

248
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:43,762
Where's Mr. Nishigami?

249
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:04,950
He's way too handsome.

250
00:13:10,581 --> 00:13:13,375
You know, Mr. Nishigami has a cool face,

251
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:16,086
but the way he talks
is actually pretty cute.

252
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:19,840
I wonder if he grew up
abroad or something?

253
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:21,091
Maybe it's a dialect?

254
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,636
There are all kinds
of people in the world.

255
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:29,850
Now then, with new members
turning up one after another,

256
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:33,979
our fortune living in this villa is…

257
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:37,316
The Grim Reaper.

258
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:49,870
<i>Oh? There are more of them?</i>

259
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:53,374
Yes.

260
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:57,670
In addition to the two people I reported
last time, three more have come.

261
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:01,632
And they will most likely…

262
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,595
stay at the villa for the summer.

263
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:09,682
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

264
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:14,645
<i>It's barely been a few decades</i>
<i>since you were assigned to Tatsumi Town,</i>

265
00:14:14,728 --> 00:14:17,898
<i>but before that, you spent</i>
<i>a lot of time in foreign countries.</i>

266
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:21,277
Before Japan, I watched over the deceased

267
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:25,072
for a long time in neighboring Korea.

268
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:27,283
<i>How is it?</i>

269
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:29,493
<i>Have you gotten used to the Japanese?</i>

270
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:32,830
<i>Still, it is something to be envious of,</i>

271
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:36,667
<i>considering we are handling</i>
<i>such heavy workloads every day like this.</i>

272
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:39,336
<i>And this year will likely be even busier.</i>

273
00:14:40,921 --> 00:14:41,964
That is true.

274
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:46,427
<i>At the end of summer,</i>
<i>this villa ground will be hit</i>

275
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:49,430
<i>by a large-scale landslide</i>
<i>disaster due to a typhoon.</i>

276
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:51,682
<i>Make sure to report the precise increase</i>

277
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:54,518
<i>or decrease in the number</i>
<i>of casualties when that happens.</i>

278
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:59,148
<i>Keep track of the people coming</i>
<i>and going from those villa grounds,</i>

279
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:00,941
<i>Grim Reaper.</i>

280
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,362
Yes, I understand.

281
00:15:06,071 --> 00:15:08,824
Until the moment
the flame of their lives goes out,

282
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:12,286
I will watch over them closely.

283
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:21,712
DOCTOR KENTARO SAWAMURA
EXTRAS WAITING AREA

284
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:26,008
That's right. A villa in Tatsumi Town.

285
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:27,968
Even when it comes to reading a script,

286
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:30,137
just getting away
from the hustle and bustle of the city

287
00:15:30,220 --> 00:15:36,810
completely changes how you play the role,
or how you build the character, you know.

288
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:38,395
Oh, really!

289
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:39,647
The three of you are cute.

290
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:41,190
I might fall in love today.

291
00:15:41,273 --> 00:15:43,108
Extras, it's almost time.

292
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:44,360
- Okay!
- Thank you.

293
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:45,277
Let's do this!

294
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:48,197
It looks like Mr. Jin can't come today.

295
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,532
- What?
- What should we do?

296
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:52,701
- What will we do?
- Why not?

297
00:15:56,747 --> 00:15:58,165
I'm sorry, everyone!

298
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:04,171
Jin Ichijo suddenly can't come,
so today's shooting is canceled!

299
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:06,131
What?

300
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:09,009
- I waited for five hours.
- I'm sorry.

301
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:10,719
Seriously?

302
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:16,558
Come on, it's not good to bail
when you're the main star.

303
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:20,938
I wonder if Mr. Jin
caught a cold or something?

304
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:32,116
Is it true that you have a villa
in Tatsumi Town?

305
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:35,744
Mr. Jin?

306
00:16:36,286 --> 00:16:39,415
Can I go there too?

307
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,042
You want to come?

308
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:43,836
Yes.

309
00:17:05,232 --> 00:17:06,525
I'm the actor…

310
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:07,860
I'm Jin Ichijo.

311
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:09,778
Why is a celebrity
coming to a place like this?

312
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,822
<i>A much longer break than you all.</i>

313
00:17:11,905 --> 00:17:14,783
Mr. Jin, don't say that, come on!
You're going to be fine!

314
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:17,286
You're here on vacation, aren't you?

315
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,455
Whoa!

316
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:22,041
Are you going to eat those?

317
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,501
<i>By the way, are you from overseas?</i>

318
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:26,211
<i>The way you talk is just kind of…</i>

319
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,964
<i>I am with this publication.</i>

320
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:30,674
What an absolute piece of garbage.

321
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:32,551
<i>There's nowhere left</i>
<i>for him to go but hell.</i>

322
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:34,428
Say it to my face!

323
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:37,306
I'm just going to say it,
but you brought this entirely on yourself!

324
00:17:38,265 --> 00:17:39,516
No!

325
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,268
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
